<report>
<title>Normal distribution (z) test - single sample</title>
<br />
<table>
<tr><td>Sample name:</td><td><in>name</in></td></tr>
<tr><td>Sample mean = </td><td><in>mean</in></td></tr>
<tr><td>Population mean =</td><td><in>pop_mean</in></td></tr>
<tr><td>Sample size n =</td><td><in>size</in></td></tr>
<tr><td>Sample sd =</td><td><in>sd</in></td></tr>
<tr><td>Population sd =</td><td><in>psd</in></td></tr>
</table>

<p><ci><in>pc</in>% confidence interval <in>for</in> = <in>from</in> to <in>to</in></ci></p>

<p>Standard normal deviate (z) = <in>z</in><br />
<pval>One sided <inp>p_1</inp></pval><br />
<pval>Two sided <inp>p_2</inp></pval></p>

<p>For lognormal data:<br />
<subtotal>Geometric mean = <in>gmean</in>  (<in>pc2</in>% confidence interval = <in>lrr</in> to <in>urr</in>)</subtotal></p>
<block name="warn">

<p><warn>WARNING: numbers too small for this test, consider using a Student t test instead</warn></p>
</block>
</report>
